        <body>
            <div xml:id="d586">

                <pb facs="1049" n="955" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg955"/>

                <head>No. 586.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lothrop to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-03-17"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 17, 1887</date>.
                        (Received April 4.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 103.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose to you an
                    article published this morning in the Journal de St. Petersburg, giving some
                    account of a proposed modification of the Russian law on the subject of
                    naturalization. I also inclose a translation of said article.</p>
                <p>I am, etc,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Geo, V. N.
                    Lothrop.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d586-a1.xml" xpointer="d586-a1"/>
